---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import InfoPage from '../components/InfoPage.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="FAQs — Ben & Caitlin · Bermuda 2027" description="Frequently asked questions for Ben & Caitlin's wedding in Bermuda, June 2027.">
  <InfoPage
    heading="FAQs"
    subheading="Frequently Asked Questions"
    intro="Everything you need to know about the wedding week ahead. If you can't find what you're looking for, just get in touch."
  >
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none font-sans text-navy/80 space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">Are there any wedding gifts?</h2>
      <p>We genuinely don't expect any gifts or contributions (we really mean it!). Travelling to Bermuda is a significant expense and we're so grateful that you're making the journey to celebrate with us.</p>
      <p>We'd much rather you spend your money on enjoying your holiday, having an extra cocktail (or two!) and making the most of your time on the island.</p>
      <p>If anyone is particularly inclined, a contribution towards our honeymoon where we eat and drink our way around Italy Stanley Tucci style, would be gratefully received. Our Joint Monzo for the trip can be provided on request.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">What is the wedding dress code?</h2>
      <p>June in Bermuda is warm (typically 26–29°C), so we'd encourage lightweight fabrics that will keep you comfortable throughout the day.</p>
      <p>For the wedding, we're looking at smart summer wedding attire. Shirts, chinos or lightweight trousers, smart shorts, summer dresses and smart footwear are all perfect. Jackets are optional and there's no need to wear a tie (or long socks!) unless you'd like to.</p>
      <p>Although the wedding itself isn't on the beach, the venue overlooks the ocean and we'll have access to the beach during the celebrations.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">Will the ceremony be outdoors?</h2>
      <p>Yes. Most of our celebrations will take place outdoors, so please bear Bermuda's warm June weather in mind when choosing your outfit. We have contingency plans if it rains!</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">What is the weather like in June?</h2>
      <p>June is one of the best times to visit Bermuda with daytime temperatures typically between 26–29°C, warm sea temperatures and plenty of sunshine. Expect warm, humid conditions—it almost always feels hotter than the weather apps suggest. While June is generally dry, there can be occasional showers so we recommend packing a light waterproof.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">How many nights would you recommend?</h2>
      <p>We've planned a few optional events before and after the wedding, so if you have the flexibility, we'd recommend allowing 4–7 nights to make the most of both the island and the celebrations. Of course, however long you're able to stay, we're simply grateful you'll be there.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">What is the currency?</h2>
      <p>Bermuda uses the Bermudian Dollar (BMD), which is fixed at 1:1 with the US Dollar (USD). Both currencies are accepted interchangeably throughout the island.</p>
      <p>We wouldn't recommend obtaining Bermudian Dollars before you travel. If you need cash, it's easy to withdraw Bermudian Dollars from local ATMs after you arrive. However, credit and debit cards are accepted almost everywhere, so many visitors find they rarely need cash.</p>
      <p>Amex is not widely accepted.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-navy">What plug sockets are used?</h2>
      <p>Bermuda uses Type A and Type B sockets (the same as the United States and Canada), operating on 120V. UK visitors will need a travel adaptor.</p>
    </div>
  </InfoPage>
</BaseLayout>
